      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-01T20:35:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For now, the best thing to do is probably just have the Bazel build pick one of these and use it implicitly. We can add the ability to configure it via Bazel later only when G3 clients need to be able to configure it.",
      "parentUuid": "4638bd79_cdd8bb1f",
      "revId": "b24f129a3a88be4b3eb573960203680eb780529f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6d8bdc3e_34c97bff",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-01T20:50:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "On second thought, it\u0027s probably better to have both the GN and Bazel version *always* compile in the high quality one (as the default, for now), and add a way to set/override that sampler.\n\nThen, spin up a CL to turn the default to the low quality one, see which tests break. Update those clients to explicitly set the sampler to the high quality one.\n\nThen, we can make each of the sampler behaviors be a \"buffet entree\" with the default being a low-quality (or no-quality?) option to reduce code size if nothing was explicitly set.\n\nThis still makes it compile/link time configurable, but it\u0027s the client who has to make sure they are compiling and depending on \"core\" and \"hq_sampler\", without introducing a back-ref linking issue where Skia depends on something it trusts the client to depend against.",
      "parentUuid": "f63251d9_ea3abddc",
      "revId": "b24f129a3a88be4b3eb573960203680eb780529f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "583f194c_e3b94a95",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5648
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-07T21:15:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The code as checked in already always has both GN and Bazel build the high quality version. *this* CL is intended to find a way to do the set/override mechanism.\n\nI have a mechanism that seems to work for GN, but don\u0027t know how to create one for Bazel. What do you suggest for that?",
      "parentUuid": "6d8bdc3e_34c97bff",
      "revId": "b24f129a3a88be4b3eb573960203680eb780529f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "07e37f3f_f489fa63",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-07T23:16:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The mechanism I would suggest has a public header which can create the high quality one and a different header for the low quality one. Then, instead of it being a static function on `SkMipmap`, it would go in those headers, in the `SkMipmaps` namespace (or similar). Then `SkMipmap::Build` should be modified to take a `SkMipmapDownSampler` (it\u0027s fine to set a default until clients are migrated to always provide one).\n\nThat will should be \"Bazel-approved\" (and GN should be fine too).",
      "parentUuid": "583f194c_e3b94a95",
      "revId": "b24f129a3a88be4b3eb573960203680eb780529f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
